1
00:00:37,040 --> 00:00:37,880
Good morning.

2
00:00:37,904 --> 00:00:39,104
Arvydas Keršys

3
00:00:39,128 --> 00:00:40,476
Please, Eglė Grėbliauskaitė.

4
00:00:40,500 --> 00:00:41,920
Hello, very nice to meet you.

5
00:00:42,121 --> 00:00:43,660
Look, what about this event?

6
00:00:43,680 --> 00:00:45,560
The permission, it's...

7
00:00:45,590 --> 00:00:46,960
Should I show you the permission?

8
00:00:47,061 --> 00:00:47,561
What?

9
00:00:47,567 --> 00:00:48,566
Should I show you the permission?

10
00:00:48,990 --> 00:00:55,640
I have another order,
to stop you from organising the event.

11
00:00:55,770 --> 00:00:58,620
Should I show you on what
grounds I was mounting?

12
00:00:58,650 --> 00:01:01,420
We know, we have that order.

13
00:01:01,450 --> 00:01:04,460
Did you really see it?
That 'you can organise the event'.

14
00:01:04,460 --> 00:01:07,180
'Have a great event'
the municipality wished me.

15
00:01:07,204 --> 00:01:08,204
But that was then.

16
00:01:08,204 --> 00:01:14,948
'According to the notification, you do not need to take any further action, you do not need a permit and you can organise the event.'

17
00:01:15,151 --> 00:01:19,557
'Have a great event.'  Gintare Makareviciene, Vilnius City Municipality, Administrative Operations Unit, Senior Specialist

18
00:01:21,720 --> 00:01:24,460
I have a permission from the municipality
to organise the event.

19
00:01:24,690 --> 00:01:27,260
It's even published on the Internet.

20
00:01:27,490 --> 00:01:29,500
When the event started on the 10th day,

21
00:01:29,801 --> 00:01:32,306
in the evening, when the scaffolding
were already assembled,

22
00:01:32,430 --> 00:01:34,160
a letter from the municipality came

23
00:01:34,290 --> 00:01:37,580
ordering to stop the event
and to dismantle.

24
00:01:38,604 --> 00:01:40,086
Now they came to dismantle.

25
00:01:41,410 --> 00:01:42,680
Are they coming to dismantle now?

26
00:01:42,781 --> 00:01:44,986
Yes, the workers already came
to dismantle.

27
00:01:45,010 --> 00:01:50,740
I informed the municipality yesterday
that dismantle work will be today.

28
00:01:50,770 --> 00:01:52,980
Okay, look, Egle,

29
00:01:53,010 --> 00:01:54,840
are you removing the scaffolding today?

30
00:01:54,841 --> 00:01:56,646
Yes, as the municipality was informed.

31
00:01:56,770 --> 00:02:02,290
But first you must remove the moss, and there are
no other options here.

32
00:02:02,320 --> 00:02:08,100
If you take this off, the monument
in moss will show.

33
00:02:08,130 --> 00:02:12,900
But the event is forbidden.

34
00:02:12,924 --> 00:02:14,424
And its disassembly is underway.

35
00:02:14,530 --> 00:02:18,140
No, you must disassembly in reverse, moss first.

36
00:02:18,240 --> 00:02:22,200
And who came up with the order of work?
Why do you have to say in which order?

37
00:02:22,230 --> 00:02:24,370
Why does the public have to see
what they might not want to see?

38
00:02:24,370 --> 00:02:26,490
Is it said that they don't have to see?

39
00:02:26,514 --> 00:02:28,980
-No, don't remove it.
-Not the black fabrick?

40
00:02:29,010 --> 00:02:30,260
Why? 

41
00:02:30,290 --> 00:02:33,580
-Simply, the monument will be seen.
-That's disassembly process.

42
00:02:33,610 --> 00:02:37,380
I am doing what I am told to do by the municipality.

43
00:02:37,410 --> 00:02:41,120
You should start with moss.

44
00:02:41,150 --> 00:02:44,900
Why not start with moss? Why?

45
00:02:44,930 --> 00:02:46,200
Why did you come

46
00:02:46,230 --> 00:02:52,240
and one introduced himself first,
and then the other, and not vice versa?

47
00:02:52,387 --> 00:02:56,300
So there is basically no difference at all.

48
00:02:56,330 --> 00:02:59,020
Whether the fabric will be removed
or moss, there's no difference.

49
00:02:59,050 --> 00:03:01,340
I am not obliged to disassemble

50
00:03:01,370 --> 00:03:05,860
without showing moss by the municipality.

51
00:03:05,890 --> 00:03:08,180
If I am, show me, please.

52
00:03:08,210 --> 00:03:10,420
Authorities will come and explain.

53
00:03:10,450 --> 00:03:13,380
When they will, then we'll do it like that.

54
00:03:13,410 --> 00:03:18,960
I told the municipality when the scaffolding will be dismantled and that's what I'm doing.

55
00:03:19,465 --> 00:03:21,380
-I'm recording.
-Okay.

56
00:03:21,410 --> 00:03:24,980
Do you have an order to stop the dismantling?

57
00:03:25,010 --> 00:03:27,220
-Of course.
-Say it.

58
00:03:27,250 --> 00:03:29,860
-Yes, I am saying it.
-Are you stopping the dismantling?

59
00:03:30,010 --> 00:03:32,860
-Yes, until the moss is removed.

60
00:03:32,890 --> 00:03:35,870
 
-You came up with a dismantling order?

61
00:03:35,870 --> 00:03:37,515
-Simply following orders.

62
00:03:37,515 --> 00:03:42,420
-Are you specifying the order of dismantling?
-What? No, I don't.

63
00:03:42,450 --> 00:03:47,180
I'm responsible for mounting, dismounting
and for leaving everything safely.

64
00:03:47,210 --> 00:03:49,700
Don't prevent me from fulfilling
my obligations.

65
00:03:49,730 --> 00:03:53,260
I am interfering because
moss should be removed fist...

66
00:03:53,290 --> 00:03:55,100
Have you decided that now?

67
00:03:55,130 --> 00:03:56,760
-No, not now.
-When, then?

68
00:03:56,761 --> 00:03:58,666
-When?
-Yes.

69
00:03:58,690 --> 00:04:01,200
It's because I have
direct instructions.

70
00:04:01,230 --> 00:04:05,260
-What were the instructions?
-That you need to remove moss first.

71
00:04:05,260 --> 00:04:07,359
I'm sorry, because the recording is in progress,

72
00:04:07,524 --> 00:04:11,594
say who, when and exactly what was ordered

73
00:04:12,141 --> 00:04:13,481
It said what I am saying.

74
00:04:13,481 --> 00:04:16,980
- I want to hear this.
-Administration will come...

75
00:04:17,416 --> 00:04:21,966
No, you're talking to me right now and
you're already influencing my actions.

76
00:04:22,132 --> 00:04:24,082
People are standing in idle.

77
00:04:24,277 --> 00:04:31,133
 
Please tell: who, when and what exactly was ordered.

78
00:04:31,720 --> 00:04:36,827
Name, date and what was said.
You don't have the document for me.

79
00:04:36,827 --> 00:04:41,202
You give me the order orally, I'm listening right now.

80
00:04:41,202 --> 00:04:43,580
Very good. It's nice.

81
00:04:43,600 --> 00:04:46,260
-Hello.
-How are you doing with the dismantlement?

82
00:04:46,280 --> 00:04:49,780
The workers came but the work is being stopped.

83
00:04:49,800 --> 00:04:52,620
Could you give me a written order, please?

84
00:04:52,640 --> 00:04:55,220
We are in the rule of law, we corresponded with you.

85
00:04:55,250 --> 00:04:57,300
I am waiting for a written document.

86
00:04:57,330 --> 00:05:00,220
Because you told me to dismantle everything.

87
00:05:00,220 --> 00:05:03,140
I told you that it will be done and its now.

88
00:05:03,160 --> 00:05:05,000
And now you're stopping my work.

89
00:05:05,100 --> 00:05:07,260
-I'm not stopping your work.
-Are you not? Can we work?

90
00:05:07,480 --> 00:05:12,060
You can start with this green cover.

91
00:05:12,090 --> 00:05:15,600
Could you please indicate
the order of disassembly in writing?

92
00:05:15,600 --> 00:05:16,514
-Yes.

93
00:05:16,514 --> 00:05:20,739
-You said there are specialists here,  can I talk to them?

94
00:05:20,739 --> 00:05:24,668
-Yes, here are the stage staff.

95
00:05:26,332 --> 00:05:37,625
[TALKS TO STAGE STAFF]

96
00:05:39,160 --> 00:05:42,700
Do you have a requirement
formulated for me?

97
00:05:42,730 --> 00:05:44,220
There is no requirement.

98
00:05:44,240 --> 00:05:46,380
Could you introduce yourself?
I'm recording.

99
00:05:46,570 --> 00:05:52,410
-It's good you're recording.
-So... you're not going to talk to me?

100
00:06:05,440 --> 00:06:09,940
It is a municipal order 
to dismantle everything, so let's start.

101
00:06:09,970 --> 00:06:13,240
No document was given to me,
people don't introduce themselves.

102
00:06:13,264 --> 00:06:15,680
 
<i>-No, you're not doing anything.</i>

103
00:06:15,680 --> 00:06:18,460
I'm asking you to give me an order.

104
00:06:18,480 --> 00:06:24,380
Penalty reports will be written for non-compliance,
if you start the event, we'll call the police.

105
00:06:24,410 --> 00:06:29,360
The legal claim from the municipality,
that I have to dismantle

106
00:06:29,390 --> 00:06:33,360
and I'm starting it now, and you're stopping it now.

107
00:06:33,360 --> 00:06:36,724
You didn't introduce yourself,
I'm guessing the claim is from you.

108
00:06:36,724 --> 00:06:40,145
-Yes, I am Gintaras Leperskas
from the municipal administration.

109
00:06:40,145 --> 00:06:43,643
-I wrote a letter to you.

110
00:06:43,643 --> 00:06:47,460
And you promised that everything will be dismantled today.

111
00:06:47,480 --> 00:06:49,580
-It will be.
-But it's not done yet.

112
00:06:49,600 --> 00:06:52,900
Disassembly is happening today and you're stopping it now.

113
00:06:53,030 --> 00:06:54,920
Today it's not dismantled yet.

114
00:06:54,920 --> 00:06:57,300
Do you give me permission to dismantle?

115
00:06:57,330 --> 00:06:59,674
Yes. Start with the green one.

116
00:07:10,760 --> 00:07:13,000
Vilnius is like a city of writers.

117
00:07:13,030 --> 00:07:18,360
There are a lot of writers.Good ones, too. 

118
00:07:18,390 --> 00:07:20,980
Did he do you anything wrong?

119
00:07:21,100 --> 00:07:25,816
-No, who says he did something wrong?
-I think you want to do something bad

120
00:07:25,816 --> 00:07:27,760
 
-No. We just want...

121
00:07:27,760 --> 00:07:29,956
You want something good? 

122
00:07:29,956 --> 00:07:32,806
We want to uncover the monument.

123
00:07:32,806 --> 00:07:37,781
But people that covered, refuse to do so.

124
00:07:39,288 --> 00:07:41,407
You said it would be dismantled today. It's not.

125
00:07:41,407 --> 00:07:43,887
Good afternoon, Jaroslavas.

126
00:07:44,440 --> 00:07:46,020
Thank you so much for answering.

127
00:07:46,040 --> 00:07:52,760
I came to dismantle the scaffolding.
As told by the municipality.

128
00:07:52,790 --> 00:07:59,020
Head of the municipal events department
have come.

129
00:07:59,040 --> 00:08:07,160
Gintaras Leperskas and also
people from the public order department

130
00:08:07,190 --> 00:08:11,132
But do not let workers to disassemble scaffolding

131
00:08:11,132 --> 00:08:15,360
 
they interfere with the dismantling order

132
00:08:15,390 --> 00:08:23,740
They don't show any documents or let workers to enter.

133
00:08:23,770 --> 00:08:27,397
Please give me advice what should I do?

134
00:08:27,397 --> 00:08:32,436
<i>Yes, for any human act on behalf of Vilnius City Municipality administration. </i>

135
00:08:32,499 --> 00:08:36,709
<i>  Vilnius City Municipality will have to answer </i>

136
00:08:36,936 --> 00:08:44,165
<i>. Well, the secondly, in this situation, their actions can be made public </i>

137
00:08:44,165 --> 00:08:49,785
 
<i>The municipality should actuate their every action, in one form or another.</i>

138
00:08:49,785 --> 00:08:55,720
<i>And if they want to ensure formalities and ensure transparency of this process</i>

139
00:08:55,720 --> 00:09:02,951
<i> that there would be no disputes in the future, also in front of the media, they should do it. </i>

140
00:09:03,080 --> 00:09:08,680
Their coming and telling me the dismantling order - is it legal?

141
00:09:08,700 --> 00:09:11,700
Because they're just saying it to me orally.

142
00:09:11,730 --> 00:09:15,145
<i> As I said, it is better to keep a record </i>

143
00:09:15,145 --> 00:09:24,093
<i> if they do not record this action, naturally, they cannot oblige you in accordance. </i>

144
00:09:24,535 --> 00:09:30,000
<i> You just need to tell the person that it will be made public, </i>

145
00:09:30,195 --> 00:09:37,784
<i> and that Municipality will carry the responsibility for the legal consequences, in accordance with the procedure established by legal acts </i>

146
00:09:38,840 --> 00:09:39,920
Thank you so much.

147
00:09:39,944 --> 00:09:41,976
<i>-Good day.</i>
-Hello.

148
00:09:42,000 --> 00:09:46,500
<i> It's Austėja Mikuckytė from the LRT.lt news. </i>

149
00:09:46,530 --> 00:09:49,780
Workers are standing, waiting and they forbid them to work.

150
00:09:49,810 --> 00:09:54,060
The head of the municipal events department is present

151
00:09:54,080 --> 00:09:59,200
and now physically prevents workers from working.

152
00:09:59,200 --> 00:10:03,660
<i>The head of the municipal events department is... Remind me? </i>

153
00:10:03,690 --> 00:10:05,480
-Would you introduce yourself?
-No.

154
00:10:07,040 --> 00:10:10,580
<i> Could I please talk to him? </i>

155
00:10:10,610 --> 00:10:13,300
Would you agree to talk? LRT?

156
00:10:13,320 --> 00:10:14,620
I have no one to talk to.

157
00:10:14,650 --> 00:10:17,425
He doesn't want to talk to you. He's standing next to me.

158
00:10:17,425 --> 00:10:20,225
-I don't know if it's LRT. I don't see anyone.

159
00:10:20,225 --> 00:10:22,620
He says he doesn't know you're from LRT

160
00:10:22,650 --> 00:10:26,180
and he doesn't see anyone. Refuses
to talk to you.

161
00:10:26,200 --> 00:10:28,760
Wait, she's introducing.

162
00:10:28,780 --> 00:10:30,530
Now one more time, okay? He can hear you.

163
00:10:30,535 --> 00:10:33,365
<i>  Austėja Mikuckytė Mateikienė </i>

164
00:10:33,370 --> 00:10:36,940
<i> from LRT.lt news, cultural section editor </i>

165
00:10:36,970 --> 00:10:41,677
-He turns and walks away. He can hear you.

166
00:10:41,677 --> 00:10:48,925
<i>  -So I'll just write that he refused to speak. </i>

167
00:10:48,925 --> 00:10:51,997
-Yes, he turned away and refused to speak.

168
00:10:51,997 --> 00:10:53,600
Don't lie, I'm on the phone.

169
00:10:53,630 --> 00:10:54,860
You're not talking anymore.

170
00:10:54,890 --> 00:10:58,641
I've got things to do. Please do not disturb me. Please.

171
00:10:58,641 --> 00:11:00,300
Well, you can hear how it is.

172
00:11:00,330 --> 00:11:02,160
<i>Yes, he has things to do.</i>

173
00:11:02,495 --> 00:11:06,000
This is not important.

174
00:11:06,394 --> 00:11:09,134
<i> So they demand to change the work order, yes? </i>

175
00:11:09,134 --> 00:11:16,907
<i> First, moss and only then scaffolding and fabric. Did I get it right? </i>

176
00:11:16,907 --> 00:11:25,025
-Yes, this is the request but it is now not possible, because scaffolding workers work only with scaffolding.

177
00:11:25,025 --> 00:11:32,840
They can't touch the sculpture and art work because I can't take responsibility for their safety.

178
00:11:32,840 --> 00:11:39,560
Yesterday the dismantling began, but the police officers kicked the moss workers out.

179
00:11:40,180 --> 00:11:45,377
If you are climbing to remove the green cover, you are welcome.

180
00:11:45,880 --> 00:11:50,000
But that's not our job. Our work is scaffolding.

181
00:11:50,000 --> 00:11:52,820
I didn't do the decor, I don't have to take it off.

182
00:11:52,840 --> 00:11:57,138
That's what we're talking about.
If you'd remove the decor,  I'd support your leg.

183
00:11:57,138 --> 00:12:01,109
 
-No, the others will come and take it down.

184
00:12:01,359 --> 00:12:05,293
-They'll be able to do it from the hoist.

185
00:12:05,293 --> 00:12:08,100
The time is running. We can not wait.

186
00:12:08,130 --> 00:12:10,860
I understand it's running. I am also wasting my time.

187
00:12:10,880 --> 00:12:13,736
Why don't you allow the dismantling of the black fabric first?

188
00:12:13,736 --> 00:12:16,822
Do you allow to take black fabric down?

189
00:12:16,846 --> 00:12:20,080
Green. Look, there is the color green, if you can see.

190
00:12:20,110 --> 00:12:24,360
Here is scaffolding now, you don't allow to dismantle them.

191
00:12:24,480 --> 00:12:26,880
We do. Remove the green cover and dismantle the scaffolding.

192
00:12:26,910 --> 00:12:30,100
-You want it to be done in that order?
-It has to be.

193
00:12:30,120 --> 00:12:31,500
Why?

194
00:12:31,530 --> 00:12:33,930
To prevent you to show what you planned.

195
00:12:33,930 --> 00:12:39,240
Show what? So the green monument won't be seen?

196
00:12:43,760 --> 00:12:47,840
Why can't you say to the camera, what have you just demanded of me?

197
00:12:49,680 --> 00:12:53,680
You don't want people to see the monument covered in green?

198
00:12:55,000 --> 00:12:58,400
Workers are standing, they are not allowed to work.

199
00:13:19,760 --> 00:13:21,700
This is called art censorship.

200
00:13:21,730 --> 00:13:27,100
In free democratic country - art censorship.

201
00:13:27,130 --> 00:13:28,340
The municipality has issued a permit.

202
00:13:28,370 --> 00:13:32,700
When the event started, stopped it and don't let to uncover, so it won't be seen.

203
00:13:33,130 --> 00:13:35,180
That's censorship, art censorship.

204
00:13:35,200 --> 00:13:36,940
-Honestly.
-Not honestly.

205
00:13:36,970 --> 00:13:40,960
Absoluttely honestly. We talked about scaffolding. I sent a press release.

206
00:13:40,961 --> 00:13:42,551
Everything. We negotiated everything.

207
00:13:42,650 --> 00:13:46,420
The municipality was friendly and very supportive.

208
00:13:46,450 --> 00:13:49,060
Except something happened when the event started.

209
00:13:49,080 --> 00:13:52,660
Could you comment on what happened?

210
00:13:52,690 --> 00:13:56,060
Leave the responsibility to me. It will be dismantled.

211
00:13:56,090 --> 00:13:58,300
-You said it will be dismantled today.
-Today it will be dismantled.

212
00:13:58,301 --> 00:14:00,906
-Nothing's done. Nothing's happening.
-It just started today.

213
00:14:00,930 --> 00:14:03,686
-Nothing's happening, Egle.
-It is. You stopped the work.

214
00:14:03,924 --> 00:14:06,256
You have now stopped the work.

215
00:14:07,320 --> 00:14:10,540
An artwork has its value.

216
00:14:10,570 --> 00:14:12,400
Both a sculpture and a work of art.

217
00:14:12,430 --> 00:14:14,860
Any people can't spoil it.

218
00:14:14,890 --> 00:14:18,500
And this piece, if your 'Grinda' will damage it, it has its value.

219
00:14:18,530 --> 00:14:21,208
It's not the first time, we've done this before.

220
00:14:21,208 --> 00:14:24,300
Censoring art not for the first time?

221
00:14:24,330 --> 00:14:26,200
-It's not art censorship.
-What is that?

222
00:14:26,920 --> 00:14:28,200
What is that?

223
00:14:39,040 --> 00:14:41,380
You give permission and take it back.

224
00:14:44,080 --> 00:14:46,750
-By whose order are we not allowed to enter?
-What is this object?

225
00:14:46,750 --> 00:14:49,060
-You are an official

226
00:14:49,080 --> 00:14:50,760
tell me officially, I need to know.

227
00:14:50,790 --> 00:14:53,424
-Are you the host of the event? -Yes.

228
00:14:53,424 --> 00:14:59,506
-Officers will give you fine for an illegal event because you said it can happen for two days. Your words.

229
00:14:59,720 --> 00:15:00,900
-Today's the third day.
-Okay.

230
00:15:00,930 --> 00:15:04,890
-Go ahead, the protocol will be written. I'll talk to you then.

231
00:15:04,890 --> 00:15:09,320
I want to know on what basis you don't allow to enter it now?

232
00:15:09,680 --> 00:15:12,640
On what grounds do you not allow to enter the object?

233
00:15:12,960 --> 00:15:16,920
Go to the officers, they will write a protocol for an illegal event.

234
00:15:16,950 --> 00:15:21,580
-Can we come in and dismantle?
-Remove the fabric.

235
00:15:21,600 --> 00:15:22,900
Can workers work?

236
00:15:22,930 --> 00:15:26,860
-Remove the fabric.
-Can they remove the scaffolding?

237
00:15:26,890 --> 00:15:29,260
-Can they remove the scaffolding?
